<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Longinus (missionary)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Longinus was a Miaphysite <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> and missionary who worked in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubia">Nubia</a> in the 6th century. Consecrated bishop for the kingdom of Nobadia in the 560s, he spent several years organising its church, and around 580 he travelled south to the kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alodia">Alodia</a>, whose king and court he baptised. His mission, described by John of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ephesus">Ephesus</a>, brought Miaphysite <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> to the court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soba">Soba</a>.</p></div>
